Chapter: PunctualLaunderAct

 Probe (closed by the punctual FIX campaign): three holes, all shut.
 CDX6004 is now an any-effect-row judgment - a punctual signature
 must be effect-free, so the custom Tick effect is rejected (its
 handler's latency is unbounded from the caller's seat). The lambda
 walk now descends into act statements, so the closure inside draws
 CDX6003. The call walk has an act arm, so the call to a
 non-punctual recursive function inside the block draws CDX6001.

Section: Effects

  effect Tick where
    tick-op : [Tick] Integer

Section: Definitions

  slow-sum : Integer -> Integer
  slow-sum (n) = if n <= 0 then 0 else n + slow-sum (n - 1)

  punctual spend : Integer -> [Tick] Integer
  spend (x) = act
   t <- tick-op
   let f = \k -> k + 1
   in f (slow-sum (t + x))
  end

  opening : Text =
   let r = with Tick (spend 5)
     tick-op (resume) = resume 3
   in show r

